# AI Usage Log 

**Tool used:** Claude (Anthropic)
**Project:** Node.js / Express / PostgreSQL User Management API

## Summary of AI Assistance

I used Claude as a debugging and reference aid while building a REST API for user
management (Express + `pg` + PostgreSQL). AI was not used to generate the project
from scratch — the routes, schema, and business logic were written independently;
AI was consulted for specific, isolated issues encountered during development.

## Interactions

1. **Fetching an array of user objects in Node.js**
   Asked for general patterns to query and return an array of user objects
   (in-memory, MongoDB, PostgreSQL, and external API approaches). Used this as a
   reference to confirm the `SELECT * FROM users` + `result.rows` pattern already
   used in the `GET /users` route was correct.

2. **Debugging: Postgres error `42703` (undefined column) on `POST /users`**
   AI traced the error to the `RETURNING` clause in the `INSERT` query referencing
   a non-existent `username` column (table only has `fullname`). Fix applied
   manually: corrected the `RETURNING` clause to reference existing columns and
   removed `password` from the returned fields.

## Verification

All AI-suggested fixes were manually reviewed, applied by hand, and tested against
the running API before being accepted — no code was copy-pasted without
understanding the underlying cause (env variable naming convention in `pg`,
column/schema mismatch).

